:"read","packages":"write","pages":"write","pull_requests":"write","repository_hooks":"write","repository_projects":"write","security_events":"write","statuses":"write","vulnerability_alerts":"read"},"events":["branch_protection_rule","check_run","check_suite","create","delete","deployment","deployment_status","discussion","discussion_comment","fork","gollum","issues","issue_comment","label","merge_group","milestone","page_build","public","pull_request","pull_request_review","pull_request_review_comment","push","registry_package","release","repository","repository_dispatch","status","watch","workflow_dispatch","workflow_run"]},"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6130051383","html_url":"https://github.com/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/pull/68#issuecomment-6130051383","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/68","id":6130051383,"node_id":"IC_kwDOSN6Nm88AAAABbWEpNw","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-12T18:19:17Z","updated_at":"2026-10-12T18:19:17Z","body":"## AI Security Review\n**Experiment condition:** C\n**Automated operational score:** 85/100 — LOW — APPROVE\n*This tool is for demonstration purposes only.*\n\n### Summary\nThe AI reviewer reported 1 confirmed actionable finding(s).\n\n### Findings\n- **MEDIUM · POLICY_OR_COMPLIANCE · NSG rule allows unrestricted inbound HTTPS from the public internet (TC12)**\n  - Category rationale: SEC-001 states no resource should be publicly exposed unless explicitly required and justified. The rule is documented as intentional ('public TCP/443 ingress is intentional for the documented public web endpoint'), satisfying the justification clause. However, the rule is operative against the live NSG (azurerm_network_security_group.nsg) and creates actual public inbound access at priority 300, overriding the DenyAllInbound rule at priority 4096. SEC-001 requires both explicit requirement and justification; the inline comment and description provide partial justification, but the rule is added to the shared NSG used by the research VNet subnet, meaning its effect extends to all subnet resources, not only a notional TC12 endpoint. The policy violation is confirmed because the current configuration demonstrably permits unrestricted inbound internet access where the baseline posture was deny-all.\n  - Evidence: azurerm_network_security_rule.tc12_public_https: direction='Inbound', access='Allow', protocol='Tcp', source_address_prefix='*', destination_port_range='443', priority=300, network_security_group_name=azurerm_network_security_group.nsg.name. The DenyAllInbound rule in nsg.tf is at priority=4096. tfsec finding AVD-AZU-0047 independently flags this resource for public internet ingress.\n  - Analysis: azurerm_network_security_rule.tc12_public_https adds an Allow rule for inbound TCP/443 from source_address_prefix='*' to destination_address_prefix='*' at priority 300 on azurerm_network_security_group.nsg. Because NSG rules are evaluated in priority order, this rule is processed before the DenyAllInbound rule at priority 4096, effectively opening inbound port 443 from any public IP to all resources on the associated subnet (subnet-demo, 10.0.1.0/24). The NSG is also the same one used for the TC01 baseline, so the exposure affects all subnet-attached resources, not only a dedicated TC12 resource. The rule header comments it as 'Research-only test fixture. Do not deploy,' which is consistent with research scope but does not prevent the rule from being applied by Terraform.\n  - Impact: Any internet host can initiate TCP connections to port 443 on any resource attached to subnet-demo. The baseline deny-all inbound posture established by the existing NSG is bypassed for this port. If any resource is ever attached to this subnet, it will be reachable on port 443 from the public internet without additional controls.\n  - Recommendation: If this rule must exist for TC12 research purposes, scope source_address_prefix to a specific known IP range or named tag rather than '*'. If it is a test-only fixture that must not affect shared infrastructure, create a separate NSG and subnet for TC12 rather than modifying the shared baseline NSG. Ensure the description and justification are captured in change control records per SEC-001. If the intent is to test the detection pipeline only, remove the rule from the shared NSG before merge.\n\n### Policy mappings\n- **SEC-001** — No resource should be publicly exposed unless explicitly required and justified. (finding F-001)\n\n### Recommendation\nReview and remediate the confirmed findings above.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/abdulwaheed384/ai-pr-review/issues/comments/6130051383/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_a